---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import workingWithMe from "../data/working-with-me.json";
---

<BaseLayout title="Working with me" sideBarActiveItemID="working-with-me">
  <div class="mb-5 mt-5">
    <div class="text-3xl font-bold">Working with me</div>
  </div>

  <section class="mb-8" aria-labelledby="phd-opportunities">
    <h2 id="phd-opportunities" class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">PhD opportunities at UCL</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-base-content/80">
      🎓 I have a fully funded PhD position available at UCL. I'm interested in two broad directions:</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal mx-6 mb-4 grid gap-4 text-base-content/80">
      <li>
        AI evaluation, auditing, and interpretability. Understanding the beliefs, goals and other internal states
        that guide neural network behaviour, and developing methods to measure and test their functional role.
        I've been working on this with controlled tasks, games, and agent environments, but I'd be also interested
        in scaling to real-world settings. Recent work:
        <a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v306/arghal26a.html" target="_blank" class="link">[1]</a>,
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.08693" target="_blank" class="link">[2]</a>,
        <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1517/" target="_blank" class="link">[3]</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Computational models of human language use. Exploring innovative ways of using neural language models
        as models of comprehension and production, ideally following recent work on incremental prediction
        and belief updates, production choice, and information contours
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jml.2025.104715" target="_blank" class="link">[4]</a>,
        <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.1814/" target="_blank" class="link">[5]</a>,
        <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-emnlp.682/" target="_blank" class="link">[6]</a>,
        <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2025.acl-long.1527/" target="_blank" class="link">[7]</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mb-4 text-base-content/80">
      The position includes 180 hours of teaching assistant duties per year,
      typically covering two courses. Recruitment for this position will be through the
      <a href="https://ellis.eu/research/phd-postdoc" target="_blank" class="link font-bold">ELLIS PhD Programme</a>.
      Applications open on 6 October 2026 and close on 31 October 2026.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4 text-base-content/80">
      <a href="https://apply.ellis.eu/" target="_blank" class="link">Apply here</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base-content/80">
      If you are eligible for UK Home fee status, let me know as there may be additional specific funding available.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="divider my-4"></div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-2xl font-bold">Funding opportunities</div>
  </div>
  <p class="mb-4 text-base-content/80">
    The strongest candidates may also be put forward for other funding programmes, including UBEL, RES, ROS and MMI, listed below.
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    {workingWithMe.opportunities.map((opp: {title: string; url: string; note?: string}) => (
      <li>
        <a href={opp.url} target="_blank" class="link">{opp.title}</a>
        {opp.note && <span class="text-base-content/60"> ({opp.note})</span>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-2xl font-bold">Application and funding information</div>
  </div>
  <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    {workingWithMe.opportunity_information.map((item: {title: string; url: string; note: string}) => (
      <li>
        <a href={item.url} target="_blank" class="link">{item.title}</a>
        <span class="text-base-content/60"> ({item.note})</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="mb-8 text-base-content/80">
    Please note that I receive a high volume of emails. I keep a record of everyone who gets in touch
    and try to read each research proposal, but I will not be able to reply to most enquiries.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
